--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/V167_GUARD_LOG_SEVERITY.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# V167 Database Guard Log Severity
+
+Release: `17.0.0-selfbuilt.167-guard-log-severity`
+
+## Change
+
+The successful Render startup message now reports `database guards 9/9 ready` without severity keywords. Render had classified the prior successful message as `critical` solely because the text contained that word, which could create a false operational alert.
+
+The database guard attestation remains unchanged: all nine PostgreSQL guards are still verified in the startup transaction before directory seeding and commit, and any drift still rolls the startup transaction back.
+
+## Scope
+
+- no database schema or backup contract change;
+- backup schema remains `0122-acceptance-ledger-integrity` with 76 tables;
+- no payment, payout, wallet, game-provider, DNS, credential, plan, or production-control change;
+- no live provider or customer transaction calls during validation.
